# Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic  
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)  
**Risk:** One branch never executes — hidden testing gap; the test "passes" regardless of which type is returned.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — if/else means the test asserts different things depending on runtime type
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests or assert unconditionally:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test  
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**Risk:** Adds 3 seconds of wall-clock time; non-deterministic — may pass/fail depending on machine speed. Still a smell even in integration tests (per calibration: delays that *wait for async coordination* are tolerable only when no polling/event alternative exists).

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Use a polling loop with timeout or an `async` event wait:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of fixed sleep
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        Assert.IsTrue(DateTime.UtcNow < deadline, "Notification not sent within timeout");
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Assertion-Free Test  
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**Risk:** False confidence — this test passes even if every insert silently fails or corrupts data. The name implies "no exception = pass" intent, but without an explicit assertion, regressions can hide.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion at all
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette  
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**Risk:** 4 assertions with no message parameters — when one fails, the test runner shows only `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no context about *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add discriminating messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are **well-designed** and exhibit no smells:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert; 2 focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion on absence — clean |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion is self-documenting (3 items just added); `CollectionAssert` use is appropriate |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate multi-threaded integration scenario with clear assertion |

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` fixture is **not** a General Fixture — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Eliminates a test that can never catch a regression |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Closes a branch that may never execute |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~5 min | Removes 3s of non-deterministic wait |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~2 min | Improves failure diagnostics |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have smells (50% infection rate, consistent with Peruma et al. prevalence data). The high-severity trio (Conditional Logic, Sleepy, Assertion-Free) are the kind correlated with flaky failures (Camara et al., SAST 2021). The remaining tests are clean and follow good integration-test conventions with the in-memory SQLite approach avoiding the Mystery Guest smell entirely.
